OL,2,V55555555CSOVIET PARLIAMENT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CAPPROVES PRIVATE LAND
OL,4,         C
OL,5, The Soviet parliament has abolished the
OL,6, collectivisation of land, passing a law
OL,7, allowing individuals to lease areas as
OL,8, part of President Gorbachev's reforms.
OL,10, But economists expressed scepticism
OL,11, over the law,saying its provisions were
OL,12, too weak to make significant changes to
OL,13, Soviet economic pratices.
OL,15, The law gives a legal framework to
OL,16, leasing arrangements which Mr Gorbachev
OL,17, hopes will boost farm production.
OL,19, The new legislation runs counter to the
OL,20, constitution which says land is "the
OL,21, exclusive property of the state".
OL,23,F]DFrom 28-02-90 / teletextarchive.com
