OL,2,V55555555CBRITAIN PLUNGES
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CDEEPER INTO RED
OL,5, Britain's trade gap widened alarmingly
OL,6, in January - a serious blow to
OL,7, Chancellor John Major ahead of next
OL,8, month's Budget.
OL,10, The current account deficit stood at
OL,11, nearly #1.9bn, compared with a
OL,12, downwardly revised December gap of
OL,13, #817m and an expected deficit of #2.2bn
OL,15, The City, however, took into account
OL,16, #500m of "erratic" items and volatile
OL,17, oil trading and was reasonably relaxed.
OL,19, Over the three months up to January the
OL,20, volume of exports was actually 4%
OL,21, higher than in the previous quarter.C>>
OL,23,F]DFrom 28-02-90 / teletextarchive.com
