OL,2,V55555555CLABOUR MOVE COULD
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSPELL END FOR BROWN
OL,4,         C
OL,5, Labour's national executive committee
OL,6, has given the go-ahead for moves which
OL,7, could result in sitting MP Ron Brown's
OL,8, de-selection.
OL,10, By a vote of 23-2, backing leader Neil
OL,11, Kinnock, the Leith constituency party
OL,12, was given the go-ahead for a special
OL,13, meeting to reconsider his reselection.
OL,15, The constituency has already passed a
OL,16, no confidence vote against Mr Brown,
OL,17, convicted of criminal damage in a court
OL,18, case and fined #1,000.
OL,20, Mr Brown is to appeal against the NEC
OL,21, decision, which he called "shamocracy".
OL,23,F]DFrom 28-02-90 / teletextarchive.com
