OL,2,V55555555CTHAMES TRAGEDY
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSISTER SHIPS SEIZED
OL,4,         C
OL,5, Two sister ships of the vessels
OL,6, involved in last summer's Marchioness
OL,7, Thames tragedy have been arrested.
OL,9, Solicitors acting for the injured and
OL,10, bereaved said they hoped the seizures
OL,11, would lead to "prompt and proper
OL,12, compensation being paid".
OL,14, Fifty-one partygoers died when the
OL,15, Marchioness, on hire for a private
OL,16, party, sank near Southwark Bridge after
OL,17, a collision with the Bowbelle.
OL,19, Warrants of arrest for the Hurlingham
OL,20, and the Bowtrader, sister ships of the
OL,21, Marchioness and the Bowbelle, were
OL,22, granted in the High Court and executed.
OL,23,F]DFrom 28-02-90 / teletextarchive.com
